WEBVTT

00:00:02.127 --> 00:00:04.129
It looks like the world is on fire.

00:00:04.212 --> 00:00:05.547
Ekpyrosis.

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:09.926
The ancient Greek Stoics believed that
the world gets destroyed in a great fire.

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:12.053
Why do you think so?

00:00:13.012 --> 00:00:17.350
Pessimists say that
the god of the universe wanted to erase

00:00:17.434 --> 00:00:19.936
all evidence of his blunder
of creating mankind,

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.397
but there's a more pragmatic reason.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:27.944
To prevent the god from getting bigger
than the universe and to start all over.

00:00:35.952 --> 00:00:37.328
It's covered in soot.

00:00:37.829 --> 00:00:39.080
Soot from the lamp.

00:00:39.956 --> 00:00:44.335
The magical lamp from the lake
was tested here 50 years ago.

00:00:44.419 --> 00:00:45.795
Experimenting with the calculator?

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:49.424
It failed, and this is the result
of a combinatorial explosion.

00:00:49.507 --> 00:00:51.718
The calculation caused an explosion?

00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:56.848
An explosive increase in combinatorics
due to the problem's growth in complexity.

00:00:57.432 --> 00:01:02.228
Massive amounts of calculations
were repeated and compressed.

00:01:02.312 --> 00:01:05.607
-Matarisvan was almost born.
-"Mata…"

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:08.526
Also known as Agni, the god of fire.

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:10.195
Like Kagutsuchi?

00:01:10.278 --> 00:01:12.781
A Japanese god whose mother died
from a burn injury

00:01:12.864 --> 00:01:14.449
when she gave birth to him.

00:01:14.949 --> 00:01:18.244
A research committee was formed,
but it got nowhere.

00:01:18.328 --> 00:01:22.290
The Super Dimension Calculator was sealed,
and 20 years passed.

00:01:22.373 --> 00:01:24.918
Then Professor Li broke the seal.

00:01:25.001 --> 00:01:29.881
This is where she discovered Archetype
as well as the Orthogonal Diagonalizer.

00:01:30.507 --> 00:01:33.635
And she relaunched
the lifting up of Singular Point.

00:01:33.718 --> 00:01:37.222
Not as a calculator
but as a production plant.

00:01:37.305 --> 00:01:38.389
Professor Li…

00:01:38.973 --> 00:01:43.645
But according to you, the calculator
gets results from the future.

00:01:43.728 --> 00:01:46.147
In other words, what happened was…

00:01:46.231 --> 00:01:51.569
Professor Ashihara reached into the future
and witnessed the Catastrophe?

00:01:51.653 --> 00:01:53.029
It seems like it.

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:57.033
If so, we should repeat
the calculation in the near future

00:01:57.117 --> 00:02:00.370
instead of reaching out
all the way to the Catastrophe.

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:02.914
Your calculation was successful,
wasn't it?

00:02:02.997 --> 00:02:05.625
You'll see when we get there.

00:02:05.708 --> 00:02:07.669
More stairs?

00:02:07.752 --> 00:02:10.547
All this force
just from a pre-engaged future?

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:14.092
Ashihara was caught
in the explosion and went missing.

00:02:14.175 --> 00:02:17.011
You're going to try
to control the lamp's genie, right?

00:02:17.095 --> 00:02:18.680
You better not screw up.

00:02:19.681 --> 00:02:22.809
If we look around,
we might find his corpse here.

00:02:22.892 --> 00:02:25.311
Is there somewhere to recharge my battery?

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:29.566
Butterfly.

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:30.817
What?

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:32.652
Butterfly… No. Moth?

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:34.195
Moth?

00:02:34.279 --> 00:02:36.614
Butterflies and moths
are both lepidopterans.

00:02:36.698 --> 00:02:41.578
They are difficult to distinguish
and their behavior differs by habitat.

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:43.413
Does it bite? Is it scary?

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:44.539
Does it bite?

00:02:44.622 --> 00:02:48.042
Don't be afraid. It just wants to play.

00:02:48.126 --> 00:02:49.794
Play? What are the rules?

00:02:49.878 --> 00:02:51.838
Rules for playing with a moth?

00:02:51.921 --> 00:02:53.298
There aren't any, right?

00:02:53.882 --> 00:02:55.300
No rules…

00:02:55.383 --> 00:02:57.051
You guys can decide.

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:04.142
I can't decide the rules. I'm sad.

00:03:04.225 --> 00:03:06.895
Because you can't decide the rules?

00:03:06.978 --> 00:03:09.480
I'm sad because it's gone.

00:04:40.697 --> 00:04:42.657
The kaijus migrating
from Europe to Africa…

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:45.410
Red Dust still remains over Central Asia…

00:04:45.493 --> 00:04:48.162
Footage from a fleet
off the shores of California…

00:04:48.246 --> 00:04:50.915
Another failure to eliminate Godzilla…

00:04:50.999 --> 00:04:54.585
Thick Red Dust is blocking
satellite images…

00:04:54.669 --> 00:04:56.421
Rodans are heading this way.

00:04:57.255 --> 00:04:59.716
The same traits as Red Dust.

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:03.428
It absorbs Red Dust and grows,
as if it were a plant.

00:05:03.511 --> 00:05:05.430
Now there's a plant kaiju as well?

00:05:06.014 --> 00:05:08.016
It's causing buildings to collapse.

00:05:08.558 --> 00:05:11.769
Experts are calling it
"the blob" or "gray goo."

00:05:11.853 --> 00:05:12.770
What do they mean?

00:05:12.854 --> 00:05:14.689
Something that can't be explained.

00:05:15.315 --> 00:05:19.944
Clusters of it make
measurements imprecise and maps distort.

00:05:20.528 --> 00:05:21.946
Does it affect the terrain?

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:26.701
Near Godzilla, the angle sum
of a triangle is less than 180.

00:05:26.784 --> 00:05:28.411
Does it distort space?

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:30.538
-Stop!
-No!

00:05:30.621 --> 00:05:32.040
I heard he was here.

00:05:32.623 --> 00:05:34.292
You can't go inside.

00:05:35.043 --> 00:05:37.295
Miho! I wanted to see you.

00:05:37.378 --> 00:05:39.797
Kanoko? What are you doing here?

00:05:39.881 --> 00:05:42.050
I have a proposal.

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:44.677
The Orthogonal Diagonalizer.

00:05:45.261 --> 00:05:47.638
It can temporarily nullify Red Dust.

00:05:47.722 --> 00:05:50.767
It was proven with the monster in India.

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:54.479
If it's detonated with a code
that's being calculated in India,

00:05:54.562 --> 00:05:57.565
it can even semi-permanently
nullify Red Dust.

00:05:58.149 --> 00:06:01.027
Something like a detonation code?

00:06:01.569 --> 00:06:05.698
We also received an email
distributed by a person named Mei Kamino.

00:06:05.782 --> 00:06:07.575
Where's the code?

00:06:07.658 --> 00:06:09.994
It should be here by now, but either

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:14.082
the calculation isn't finished
or communication lines are down.

00:06:14.665 --> 00:06:18.586
How long do we wait?
Should we try a random code?

00:06:18.669 --> 00:06:22.048
The wrong code will make it
turn into ash and water.

00:06:22.131 --> 00:06:26.511
The number of possible codes is the same
as the number of particles in space.

00:06:27.303 --> 00:06:29.180
We'll never get it right by coincidence.

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:34.852
We can wait and miss our chance to use it
or use it now as a temporary solution.

00:06:34.936 --> 00:06:40.483
Kamino said you should contact Yun Arikawa
of Otaki Factory for any questions.

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:44.237
Otaki Factory…
I hear that name a lot. Where is he?

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:45.738
In Tokyo.

00:06:45.822 --> 00:06:49.117
My colleague is supposed to be with him.

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:52.411
Did Professor Ashihara's experiment
cause this?

00:06:52.495 --> 00:06:54.539
No. I did this.

00:06:54.622 --> 00:06:55.998
You detonated it.

00:06:56.082 --> 00:07:00.753
I used Ashihara's code,
but the crystallization was too unstable.

00:07:01.462 --> 00:07:04.090
What's restraining the monster
above the ground?

00:07:04.173 --> 00:07:05.758
An upgraded version.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:11.055
I used the same code
but modified the trap based on experience.

00:07:11.139 --> 00:07:12.265
Then…

00:07:12.348 --> 00:07:14.142
It's a matter of time.

00:07:14.225 --> 00:07:19.689
A few weeks or days or hours.
It will start heading to SHIVA.

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:23.484
We have to complete
the Orthogonal Diagonalizer by then.

00:07:23.568 --> 00:07:27.113
-How about looping the reaction?
-The current code won't do it.

00:07:27.196 --> 00:07:30.533
We need another one
to trigger a chain reaction.

00:07:30.616 --> 00:07:32.869
I'm making a shortlist of possible codes.

00:07:32.952 --> 00:07:35.872
What if the reaction doesn't stop?

00:07:35.955 --> 00:07:41.878
I'll go down in history as the man
who buried the world in Red Dust crystals.

00:07:41.961 --> 00:07:45.465
Maybe you're going
to cause the Catastrophe.

00:07:45.548 --> 00:07:48.050
Too much or too little of anything is bad.

00:07:48.134 --> 00:07:49.677
The good is somewhere in between.

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:52.930
If I fail, history itself
might not exist anymore.

00:07:53.014 --> 00:07:54.640
That's so irresponsible.

00:07:54.724 --> 00:07:57.143
A robot with a sense of responsibility?

00:08:00.229 --> 00:08:04.609
I at least have a conscience
of what's right and wrong.

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:07.778
A circuit with a conscience.

00:08:09.947 --> 00:08:12.408
The expiration date was 30 years ago.

00:08:12.492 --> 00:08:14.869
Don't worry about it. It's still edible.

00:08:15.745 --> 00:08:17.580
Here we go.

00:08:19.081 --> 00:08:21.417
Access granted with the ID they gave us.

00:08:21.501 --> 00:08:23.127
Oh, yes. I see.

00:08:23.211 --> 00:08:25.463
Can you do it without being detected?

00:08:25.546 --> 00:08:28.007
I temporarily shut down the alarm system.

00:08:28.090 --> 00:08:29.258
Ready?

00:08:39.852 --> 00:08:41.187
It's still stuck.

00:08:41.270 --> 00:08:43.189
Jet Jaguar, help us.

00:08:43.272 --> 00:08:44.398
I'll help.

00:08:47.026 --> 00:08:47.860
Thank you!

00:08:48.528 --> 00:08:50.238
In any case, what's happening?

00:08:50.988 --> 00:08:52.907
Is the ecosystem getting overwritten?

00:08:53.491 --> 00:08:57.078
Is Godzilla altering the environment
to build its nest?

00:08:57.161 --> 00:08:59.622
More like an invasive foreign species.

00:09:00.206 --> 00:09:03.668
Like the red-eared slider and coypu?
Can't we all coexist?

00:09:03.751 --> 00:09:06.128
There's only room for one in a niche.

00:09:06.796 --> 00:09:08.923
Maybe we're the foreign species.

00:09:09.006 --> 00:09:11.634
And Godzilla's evolution is speeding up.

00:09:11.717 --> 00:09:16.013
We can't win at this rate.
History might get rewritten.

00:09:16.097 --> 00:09:18.307
I won't allow it!

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:20.977
What's wrong, Jet Jaguar?

00:09:21.602 --> 00:09:22.436
A bird…

00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:23.688
Do you see something?

00:09:27.316 --> 00:09:28.150
Hey!

00:09:30.027 --> 00:09:31.028
What happened?

00:09:33.281 --> 00:09:34.740
It found something.

00:09:41.789 --> 00:09:43.332
A chase?

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:52.049
We must have invaded their territory.

00:09:56.178 --> 00:09:57.972
Hold your fire! It will only attract more!

00:10:08.816 --> 00:10:09.734
Take cover!

00:10:46.270 --> 00:10:47.438
Amazing.

00:10:48.022 --> 00:10:50.107
Where's your master?

00:10:52.151 --> 00:10:53.527
Mama is over there.

00:11:00.242 --> 00:11:01.369
Sato?

00:11:03.412 --> 00:11:06.957
A record of BB's shipment
of antique silverware.

00:11:07.041 --> 00:11:09.543
By cash on delivery
to embassies in seven countries.

00:11:09.627 --> 00:11:11.629
He's incorrigible.

00:11:11.712 --> 00:11:13.547
The board wants an explanation.

00:11:14.131 --> 00:11:15.925
Forget about those geezers.

00:11:16.008 --> 00:11:17.259
Security sent us a report.

00:11:17.343 --> 00:11:19.929
The crystals around Salunga
are starting to collapse.

00:11:20.888 --> 00:11:22.056
Already?

00:11:30.398 --> 00:11:32.775
We'll find the code at SHIVA.

00:11:32.858 --> 00:11:36.821
We'll also secure a network
and send it to the designated addresses.

00:11:36.904 --> 00:11:38.656
We'll get rid of Red Dust.

00:11:38.739 --> 00:11:41.492
Tilda will turn pale. We'll escape.

00:11:41.575 --> 00:11:44.453
Escape? Back to the way we came?

00:11:44.537 --> 00:11:48.457
If we succeed, Steven will help us.
We'll go out the front door.

00:11:48.541 --> 00:11:54.088
As heroes that saved the Earth,
we'll get a trophy and drink champagne.

00:11:55.423 --> 00:11:59.051
After that, we can monitor
the Catastrophe to our heart's content.

00:12:02.430 --> 00:12:05.641
Is the Singular Point in that donut?

00:12:05.724 --> 00:12:11.355
It's like a point, a line, and a ring
all at the same time.

00:12:11.939 --> 00:12:15.359
SHIVA is like an Archetype barrier
around Singular Point

00:12:15.443 --> 00:12:18.362
that also functions as a monitoring
and controlling device.

00:12:19.989 --> 00:12:25.494
Let me introduce you to SHIVA,
the heart of Union Compound India.

00:12:26.912 --> 00:12:28.873
Distorted space?

00:12:28.956 --> 00:12:31.083
Swirling like it's underwater.

00:12:31.167 --> 00:12:33.377
I think we'll get along just fine.

00:12:33.461 --> 00:12:35.754
Be careful. The left side is…

00:12:35.838 --> 00:12:37.214
Hey, watch out!

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:45.973
That was close!

00:12:53.439 --> 00:12:55.691
I almost died.

00:12:56.275 --> 00:12:57.485
But you're a robot.

00:12:57.568 --> 00:13:02.281
If I die, my backup that
I saved in Dubai will wake up somewhere.

00:13:02.364 --> 00:13:04.241
We'll have to get reacquainted.

00:13:04.325 --> 00:13:07.786
-We can skip the self-introductions.
-Over there!

00:13:08.787 --> 00:13:10.664
The swirling is stronger now.

00:13:13.626 --> 00:13:17.922
"Sent to you in loving memory
of my dear friend Guiying Li."

00:13:18.547 --> 00:13:21.342
"Please await further notice
on the funeral dress code."

00:13:21.425 --> 00:13:25.304
"May her soul rest in peace.
Bearach Byrne."

00:13:25.888 --> 00:13:27.806
This is the Orthogonal Diagonalizer?

00:13:27.890 --> 00:13:32.770
Kamino said you would know
how to use it. That terminal…

00:13:33.896 --> 00:13:35.189
It's lighter than I thought.

00:13:35.272 --> 00:13:38.067
Don't be so rough with it.
It's a bomb, right?

00:13:38.150 --> 00:13:41.570
It was in Ashihara's notes.
It's a programmable atom.

00:13:41.654 --> 00:13:44.323
-Be careful with it.
-Do you know how to use it?

00:13:44.907 --> 00:13:46.325
The structure is simple.

00:13:46.408 --> 00:13:49.828
But it's designed
so that not anybody can handle it.

00:13:51.580 --> 00:13:52.831
What's the code?

00:13:52.915 --> 00:13:54.917
Haven't you received it?

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:55.834
Received it?

00:13:55.918 --> 00:13:59.255
Is the code the final message from Kamino?

00:13:59.338 --> 00:14:00.589
It's a strong possibility.

00:14:01.173 --> 00:14:02.591
You're supposed to receive it?

00:14:03.342 --> 00:14:08.472
A message from Mei Kamino today at
9:30 a.m., 100 meters above Tokyo Station.

00:14:08.556 --> 00:14:11.267
Four hours from now.
How is she going to send it?

00:14:11.850 --> 00:14:12.726
I don't know.

00:14:13.310 --> 00:14:16.397
The time and place
were predicted over 50 years ago.

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:18.732
But that's all the information we have.

00:14:18.816 --> 00:14:20.526
Tell me in more detail.

00:14:21.026 --> 00:14:22.361
It's a long story.

00:14:22.945 --> 00:14:24.780
Can we trust the prediction?

00:14:25.281 --> 00:14:26.657
We'll take that.

00:14:26.740 --> 00:14:29.577
Once you get the code, we'll verify it--

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:30.578
There's no time.

00:14:31.328 --> 00:14:35.249
The Catastrophe itself
might also begin in four hours.

00:14:35.332 --> 00:14:37.626
The Catastrophe mentioned in the email?

00:14:37.710 --> 00:14:40.754
Godzilla destroying the universe?
You expect us to believe that?

00:14:40.838 --> 00:14:42.756
Don't think too hard about it.

00:14:43.340 --> 00:14:47.428
You're either in or not. We're in.
What about you guys?

00:14:48.971 --> 00:14:52.933
Your cooperation has been invaluable.
You've earned our trust.

00:14:53.017 --> 00:14:54.268
But there's one problem.

00:14:55.352 --> 00:14:59.273
This was Tokyo Station yesterday.
Godzilla hasn't moved all day.

00:14:59.857 --> 00:15:02.067
A hundred meters over Godzilla.

00:15:02.151 --> 00:15:06.030
It's been growing
and is now over 100 meters in height.

00:15:06.113 --> 00:15:07.781
The target is…

00:15:08.365 --> 00:15:10.618
Godzilla itself.

00:15:10.701 --> 00:15:11.702
Perfect.

00:15:11.785 --> 00:15:16.665
The Orthogonal Diagonalizer has
to be detonated in thick Red Dust.

00:15:16.749 --> 00:15:20.044
How will you get the code
that's going to be delivered there?

00:15:20.127 --> 00:15:22.546
We'll handle it.

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:26.800
Time to deploy the Godzilla slayer.

00:15:27.593 --> 00:15:30.304
Let's hope SHIVA is in a good mood.

00:15:30.387 --> 00:15:32.056
Secure external communication.

00:15:32.139 --> 00:15:33.557
You got it.

00:15:33.641 --> 00:15:35.059
Here.

00:15:36.018 --> 00:15:37.603
Hello there.

00:15:37.686 --> 00:15:41.065
Starting search for external connection.

00:15:43.651 --> 00:15:45.819
External connection secured.

00:15:46.487 --> 00:15:48.322
Can we transmit to Tokyo?

00:15:48.405 --> 00:15:51.116
We're still waiting
for a connection beyond the facility.

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:52.826
Searching satellite connection.

00:15:52.910 --> 00:15:56.455
Wait until the last minute.
We don't want Tilda to notice.

00:15:56.538 --> 00:15:57.790
The backup?

00:15:59.959 --> 00:16:02.461
It's still not possible here.

00:16:04.046 --> 00:16:07.049
I narrowed it down to three million codes.

00:16:07.132 --> 00:16:09.218
Now the simulations…

00:16:09.301 --> 00:16:11.470
There are more like three billion codes.

00:16:11.553 --> 00:16:15.224
You're kidding. Too much noise?
Mechanical malfunction?

00:16:15.307 --> 00:16:18.352
More and more possible codes
are being suggested.

00:16:19.395 --> 00:16:22.731
It won't stop.
It's increasing exponentially.

00:16:23.440 --> 00:16:25.609
The distortion is getting stronger?

00:16:25.693 --> 00:16:27.361
Can you identify the cause?

00:16:27.444 --> 00:16:30.614
There's an apparent lineage relationship
among the new codes.

00:16:30.698 --> 00:16:32.908
The task branches off in the future?

00:16:32.992 --> 00:16:37.371
From the increase in possible results
of different versions of the future.

00:16:37.454 --> 00:16:41.375
The task for finding the code
branches off from here.

00:16:41.959 --> 00:16:43.627
Is the future wavering?

00:16:43.711 --> 00:16:47.006
Can you bring the branch closer in?

00:16:47.089 --> 00:16:49.383
That should prevent the increase.

00:16:49.466 --> 00:16:50.676
You got it.

00:16:50.759 --> 00:16:53.512
The calculation distance will be reduced,
but the increase…

00:16:54.972 --> 00:16:58.475
More possible codes.
The various tasks are clashing.

00:16:58.559 --> 00:17:00.352
What's going on?

00:17:00.436 --> 00:17:02.771
I'll go closer and check.

00:17:03.981 --> 00:17:05.899
The future branches off and clashes.

00:17:05.983 --> 00:17:08.652
Even in such a near future?

00:17:11.488 --> 00:17:15.993
Swimming…

00:17:21.165 --> 00:17:25.502
The kaiju advances slowly
as it turns the city red.

00:17:25.586 --> 00:17:28.922
Sounds of firearms from military troops…

00:17:29.006 --> 00:17:30.049
It's coming this way.

00:17:30.132 --> 00:17:32.551
It's going towards SHIVA,
just as we expected.

00:17:33.052 --> 00:17:35.179
The Orthogonal Diagonalizer?

00:17:35.262 --> 00:17:37.056
One is ready to be fired.

00:17:49.818 --> 00:17:52.738
Three hours to three months?
Are you serious?

00:17:53.322 --> 00:17:54.156
What does that mean?

00:17:54.239 --> 00:17:56.742
-The Catastrophe is causing this.
-Catastrophe?

00:17:56.825 --> 00:18:02.748
I calculated the time to the Catastrophe
based on how the future is branching off.

00:18:02.831 --> 00:18:07.753
It might even happen in three hours,
not centuries from now.

00:18:07.836 --> 00:18:09.505
You were right.

00:18:09.588 --> 00:18:11.381
The Catastrophe might happen any minute?

00:18:12.341 --> 00:18:15.302
There's no time to calculate the code.

00:18:15.385 --> 00:18:17.513
We have to find a way
to stop the Catastrophe.

00:18:17.596 --> 00:18:19.515
Is there a way?

00:18:19.598 --> 00:18:21.725
Is the world coming to an end?

00:18:22.518 --> 00:18:24.019
I'm back.

00:18:24.103 --> 00:18:28.023
I'm sorry I took so long.
How many hours has it been?

00:18:28.107 --> 00:18:29.650
Only five or six minutes.

00:18:30.859 --> 00:18:34.780
I see. Time flows differently over there.

00:18:34.863 --> 00:18:37.533
-You saw the future.
-What?

00:18:37.616 --> 00:18:42.037
Am I going down in history
as the first AI to travel through time?

00:18:42.121 --> 00:18:43.747
So what did you see?

00:18:43.831 --> 00:18:45.165
Something like this.

00:18:48.627 --> 00:18:51.046
The diagram in Professor Ashihara's notes.

00:18:51.130 --> 00:18:55.801
His notes titled, "Observations
on Creatures Based on Red Dust."

00:18:55.884 --> 00:18:57.094
Is this it?

00:18:59.388 --> 00:19:00.639
Wait. That page…

00:19:00.722 --> 00:19:02.307
Does it mean…

00:19:03.100 --> 00:19:04.059
Can you read it?

00:19:04.143 --> 00:19:09.815
Was he trying to use the Orthogonal
Diagonalizer to prevent the Catastrophe?

00:19:10.524 --> 00:19:12.442
This must be his notes on it.

00:19:12.526 --> 00:19:14.820
Pelops II, search for relevant pages.

00:19:14.903 --> 00:19:16.071
Roger that.

00:19:17.656 --> 00:19:19.908
It's bigger than anything before.

00:19:22.161 --> 00:19:23.829
I found something.

00:19:23.912 --> 00:19:25.706
-I couldn't find anything.
-Nothing.

00:19:25.789 --> 00:19:27.166
Here it is.

00:19:27.249 --> 00:19:28.125
Pelops II?

00:19:28.208 --> 00:19:29.585
Is it also branching off?

00:19:29.668 --> 00:19:31.336
That's not right.

00:19:31.420 --> 00:19:35.299
-You're a liar.
-Everyone's lying except me.

00:19:35.382 --> 00:19:36.383
Yes.

00:19:37.092 --> 00:19:39.094
I see something…

00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:42.806
Pelops II!

00:19:42.890 --> 00:19:43.849
What happened?

00:19:49.021 --> 00:19:50.480
This song…

00:19:50.564 --> 00:19:51.940
It's coming from SHIVA.

00:20:49.456 --> 00:20:51.917
Silkworms… Giant silkworm moths.

00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:53.961
But their colors are different.

00:20:55.462 --> 00:21:01.051
"The flight of yellow butterflies
is a sign of warfare."

00:23:30.867 --> 00:23:35.872
Subtitle translation by: Annie Iwasaki
